# 2026-05-07 (NORA #28) — frontend build outputs are committed on this branch.
# See docs/COMMIT-BUILD-PATTERN.md in neoffice-devops.
# (pos_next writes vite output to public/pos/, not public/frontend/.)
# Build artifacts
#//// Neoffice — upstream ignores pos_next/public/pos/, pos_next/www/ and yarn.lock (built
#//// output is rebuilt on each site). We commit the build instead: c06b77e4 (2026-05-07
#//// "commit built frontend so instances pull, no rebuild on prod") — a fleet instance pulls
#//// ready-made assets, and f38e0911 makes `yarn build` a no-op when they are present because
#//// rebuilding the SPA during `bench build` gets OOM-killed on a 4 GB tenant. yarn.lock is
#//// un-ignored for POS/ by 7247a237 (2026-05-28): without it each CI run resolved different
#//// upstream versions, and a frappe-ui bump silently broke input clicks (Radix Vue Dialog
#//// focus trap) only on rebuild. The three upstream rules survive as the commented-out lines
#//// below — kept visible so the next merge sees what was disabled and why.
# pos_next/public/pos/
# pos_next/www/
# yarn.lock IS committed for POS/ — see fix below.
# Ignoring it caused non-reproducible builds: each CI run could install a
# different upstream version (e.g. frappe-ui upgrades) that introduced
# regressions only on rebuild (Radix Vue Dialog focus trap blocked input clicks).
# 2026-05-28: commit POS/yarn.lock + CI uses --frozen-lockfile.
!POS/yarn.lock
package-lock.json

